      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ultimately, the IJ held Mr. Alcaraz-Enriquez ineligible for relief, relying in part on the version of events in the probation report."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cb3fc816df2096195f2b8ee562f14a42eed48236d1f9158b6e39a9c6729744b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cb3fc816df20-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the INA provides that a reviewing court must accept \u201cadministrative fndings\u201d as \u201cconclusive unless any reasonable adjudicator would be compelled to conclude to the contrary.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cb3fc816df2096195f2b8ee562f14a42eed48236d1f9158b6e39a9c6729744b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cb3fc816df20-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the INA provides that \u201ca petition for review . . . shall be the sole and exclusive means for judicial review of an order of removal.\u201d 8 U. S. C. \u00a7 1252(a)(5)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Alcaraz-Enriquez and Mr. Dai",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cb3fc816df2096195f2b8ee562f14a42eed48236d1f9158b6e39a9c6729744b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cb3fc816df20-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because neither the IJ nor the BIA made an explicit adverse credibility determination about their testimony, Mr. Alcaraz-Enriquez and Mr. Dai say they were statutorily entitled to a presumption of credibility in their BIA appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cb3fc816df2096195f2b8ee562f14a42eed48236d1f9158b6e39a9c6729744b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cb3fc816df20-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Accordingly, the judgments of the Court of Appeals are vacated, and these cases are remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
    }
  ],
